                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2844: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-28T15:00:00+01:00">August 28, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 28—11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>348. My 342, August 22, 9 a.m. Communiqué issued this afternoon states that by
                    means of appropriate ministerial measures adopted by agreement among the
                    interested administrations the exportations direct and indirect, the
                    reexportation and transit to Spain, the Spanish possessions and the Spanish zone
                    of Morocco of arms, munitions and war materials, as well as airplanes assembled
                    or nonassembled, and war vessels have been forbidden. The communiqué adds that
                    this prohibition applies to all contracts in course of execution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
